%N A249383 Smallest odd prime number Q such that Q*2^P(n)-1 is also prime, where P(n) is the Mersenne prime exponent A000043(n).
%C A249383 The prime that corresponds to a(32) is a 227838-digit certified prime.
%C A249383 Does a(n) exist for each n? - _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Oct 28 2014
%t A249383 a[n_] := Module[{p = MersennePrimeExponent[n], q = 3}, While[! PrimeQ[q*2^p - 1], q = NextPrime[q]]; q]; Array[a, 20] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 22 2026 *)
%o A249383 (PARI) lista(nn) = {vmp = readvec("b000043.txt"); for (n=1, nn, k=2; while(!isprime(prime(k)*2^vmp[n]-1), k++); print1(prime(k), ", "););} \\ _Michel Marcus_, Oct 27 2014
%Y A249383 Cf. A000043, A249382, A249384.
%K A249383 nonn,more,changed
%O A249383 1,1
